set -eu
# The same two-hour gap against a host that would not answer: `pmset` exits non-zero. The message
# goes out, as it must, and it says which doubt this was — "the sleep history could not explain it
# (history-unreadable), which is not a claim that the host stayed awake". The event carries
# `host.assessed: unknown` with the reason, so the log says the same thing the Mac said.
#
# This is the fallback the whole design turns on. If macOS stops retaining this history, or renames
# a domain, or a later version refuses the read in a LaunchAgent, every gap lands here: visible,
# notified, and honest about what was not established. It never lands on silence.
"$BATON" tick
echo
"$BATON" status
